<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19800" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Grādīvus</span></b>  (once <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Grădīvus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6,
		427</span></i>), i, m.
		perh. from gradior, he who steps forth, marches out, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a surname of
			Mars</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(Numa) Salios item duodecim Marti Gradivo
					legit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					1, 20, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rex Gradive,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 10, 542</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Nymphas venerabar agrestes Gradivumque patrem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 35</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Homericus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					13, 113</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jure venis, Gradive,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					2, 861</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Juv. 2, 128</span></i>; so <i>absol.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Gradivus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 3, 677</span></i>
			; 5, 556; <i><span class="en">id. M. 14, 820</span></i>; <i><span class="en">15, 863</span></i>.</div>
